A||N||4||johnsimon||Help with deck light||||12||
Z||000000||johnsimon||12-07-2001||05:00 PM||||My first question here.<BR>I have an 85 GT and everything works and all is great.  But the deck light, the one by the spare tire does not work.  The buld is fine....I checked the switch, there is no voltage at the switch.  The fuse is fine as everything else on this fuse works.  Can anyone suggest where I might look next?<BR>Thanx<P>------------------<BR>John Simon<BR>johnsimon@macconn<BR>ect.com||||reg||12
Z||000001||Dan010||12-07-2001||05:05 PM||||Did you check it with the lights turned on or off, if I remember correctly, this light only turns on when the lights are turned on.<BR>Not when the lid is opened as with the engine<BR>bay lid.||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnsimon||12-07-2001||05:14 PM||||Holy crap!!!<P>A big big thank you,  I checked with the lights on and it does come on.  Now I feel better.<P>------------------<BR>John Simon<BR>johnsimon@macconn<BR>ect.com||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rumor||12-12-2001||10:51 PM||||that's weird, right? it took me awhile before I was able to figure that out. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||12-12-2001||11:06 PM||||I believe I looked at the wiring diagram in my 87 Helm manual, and it shows that it's supposed to be wired to come on through the hood pin switch.  But, we all know that this is incorrect.  So, somewhere when the wiring harnesses were assembled there was a mistake, or they simply did a last minute revisal of the schematic.  [i]Why[\i] they would wire it ack-basswards like that is beyond me. <P>I do know that that circuit is known to have some flakey grounds too, I've had to give the bulb socket a new ground on mine and I believe another Fiero...||||reg||1
